		(uuid "b53e9d9b-3e72-4372-8f0a-f675d60364e3")
	)
	(text "SYSTEM OVERVIEW\n\nASTRELIS NAV (SWARM PCB) is the electronics stack for an autonomous underwater vehicle\n(AUV) intended to operate as part of a swarm. It senses its own orientation, motion,\nand depth (Sensor board), processes this data and runs navigation/control logic\n(Control board), communicates with other units or a base station acoustically via an\nunderwater piezo transducer (TX/RX board), drives its motors/servos/lights for\npropulsion and steering (Output board), and is powered from an onboard battery with\nregulated multi-rail power distribution (Power board) — all built as a compact\nstacked-board assembly suited to a small underwater housing."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 18.288 33.274 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2.032 2.032)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "0939a733-50b7-475f-8361-e69398d5852e")
	)
	(text "for testing"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 14.478 136.398 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "13724c71-c67c-45eb-8f27-7caaceff6c6e")
	)
	(text "DUPLICATE FOOTPRINTS BETWEEN BOARDS"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 124.714 191.516 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "19fb9fa6-2933-42c4-80c4-d9871f9feee3")
	)
	(text "HEADER_PINS — Test/Probe Access\n\nBreaks out stacking connector signals (J25–J28) to accessible pins for\nbench testing, mirroring each board's header pinout (3.3V, GND, GPIO,\ncomms lines) without altering the signal path — lets you probe\ninter-board signals without disassembling the stack."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 55.626 119.634 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.524 1.524)
			)
		)
		(uuid "3e0faa4f-50ab-4698-802f-848decfc1a1d")
	)
	(text "SENSOR — Motion & environmental sensing\n\nI2C cluster: two IMUs (ASM330LHHXTR, LSM6DSO32TR), a\nmagnetometer(MMC5603NJ), and a depth/pressure sensor\n(MS583730BA01-50). Shares one I2C bus with interrupt lines\nback to Control, which it feeds with orientation/environmental data."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 236.982 89.916 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.524 1.524)
			)
		)
		(uuid "4be27fe9-d041-4153-8466-efc3a89c5bf3")
	)
	(text "Splitting SWARM into five functional boards (Control, Power, Sensor, TX/RX, Output)\nstacked via headers — rather than one monolithic board or fully separate,\nindividually-housed boards — balances modularity with integration:\n\n\nNoise isolation - Power (switching regulators) and TX/RX (sensitive RX analog, H-bridge) are separated\nfrom Sensor/Control, with isolated GND domains joined only at the stack connectors, limiting noise coupling.\n\nCompact footprint - Stacking keeps the assembly small and tube-friendly, ideal for a compact vehicle.\n\nSimple interconnect - Shared 47-pin headers pass signals board-to-board, avoiding custom wiring harnesses.\n\nModularity - Any board can be revised, repaired, or swapped independently without redesigning the whole system.\n\nEasier fab/test - Each board can be built and tested on its own before final stack assembly."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 19.05 81.026 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.778 1.778)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "4c4ecc0f-4d17-4559-8efd-c606fd58725b")
	)
	(text "POWER — Energy management\n\nTakes battery input (XT30, 4S2P pack) with surge/reverse protection,\nregulates to 3.3V, 5V, and 12V via buck converters, plus a\nboosted VPiezo rail (TPS55340) for the transducer. Includes\nvoltage-divider power monitoring, status LEDs, and supplies\npower-good signals to the rest of the stack."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 237.236 60.198 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.524 1.524)
			)
		)
		(uuid "60f5e037-60c3-4c3b-9ec7-ef51cce272e9")
	)
	(text "stacking connections between boards"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 100.838 116.078 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "679e2ed8-1f0c-41b0-9b3b-7fdac86820cd")
	)
	(text "BOARD BREAKOUTS"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 14.224 133.604 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2.54 2.54)
				(thickness 0.508)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "780493c5-5a43-43db-a8e5-0a9a7b8de001")
	)
	(text "GND DOMAIN ARCHITECTURE\nEach subsystem has an isolated GND domain: GND_POWER,\nGND_CONTROL, GND_SENSOR, GND_TXRX, GND_HEADER. These\ndomains are connected through the stacking connector\npins. No single star point."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 15.494 185.166 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "a3f1c820-5d4e-4b91-8e7a-2c6d9f0e1b47")
	)
	(text "OUTPUT — Actuation\n\nBreaks out GPIO to ESC, servo, and light headers (5V rail,\nper-channel pull resistors), routing Control's commands to\nmotors/actuators to actually move the vehicle."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 237.236 148.844 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.524 1.524)
			)
		)
		(uuid "c7b60f81-e8f1-4a90-a17d-8b992f06ad73")
	)
	(text "CONTROL — System brain\n\nSTM32F446RET6 + Raspberry Pi Pico 2 run main flight logic and \nhigher-level processing. Includes USB-C input (with ESD protection),\nmicroSD logging, SWD programming header, RGB/status LEDs,\n16MHz/32.768kHz crystals, and a boot-mode jumper for the Pico."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 237.236 29.718 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.524 1.524)
			)
		)
		(uuid "e6d20115-9501-4bfd-9be6-ce3898d8d765")
	)
	(text "TX/RX — Acoustic communication\n\nTwo half-bridge MOSFET drivers (UCC27211) form an H-bridge\ndriving the piezo transducer to transmit, with a precharge\nsequence at power-up. On receive, a preamp/instrumentation amp\n(INA823) and bandpass filter (20–30kHz, for FSK) feed a comparator;\na T/R switch (ADG7421) isolates TX/RX paths, and an INA240 senses\nH-bridge current."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 236.982 119.634 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.524 1.524)
			)
		)
		(uuid "f129903d-8341-4ebc-9c55-c60d301d4d51")
	)
	(text "HEADER PINS"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 100.584 113.284 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2.54 2.54)
				(thickness 0.508)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "f828dd2a-267e-41ac-a6bb-c56310758856")
	)
	(text "PWR FLAGS"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 76.454 178.054 0)
		(effects
